<title>LITHUANIA: LITIMPEKS SAYS 7 MO 3.32 MLN LITAS LOSSES.</title>
<headline>LITIMPEKS SAYS 7 MO 3.32 MLN LITAS LOSSES.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first seven months of 1997</p>
<p>(all amounts in million litas unless othervise stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss			 3.32  vs net profit 267,000</p>
<p>    Assets			 171.32  vs		170.9</p>
<p>    Loan portfolio	     121.16  vs		124.61</p>
<p>    Deposits and LC	    114.62  vs		144.65</p>
<p>    Corporate deposits	  19.09  vs		 54.0</p>
<p>    Individual deposits	 17.43  vs		 24.48</p>
<p>Notes - The comparison figures for assets, loan portfolio</p>
<p>and deposits and letters of credit are as of the beginning of</p>
<p>1997.</p>
<p>Litimpeks Bank reported 4.23 million litas losses for the</p>
<p>first half of 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;The bank plans to have profit in the third and the fourth</p>
<p>quarters of the year and to have one million litas profit in</p>
<p>1997,&quot; the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Litimpeks bank was shut at the beginning of a banking</p>
<p>crisis in late 1995 and was reopened in June 1996.</p>
<p>The total share capital of the bank is 64.09 million litas.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
